{"id":41298,"title":"Seamless Multiresolution Isosurfaces Using Wavelets","url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/","final_url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/m2/1/high_res_d/754498.pdf","year":2000,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"2a5e14512c4ea51a2bbd394632273d3447908ad04175c1c3d3f9cbdef5646c56","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793057298.1946697,"text_chars":46963,"abstract":"Data sets that are being produced by today's simulations, such as the ones generated by DOE's ASCI program, are too large for real-time exploration and visualization. Therefore, new methods of visualizing these data sets need to be investigated. The authors present a method that combines isosurface representations of different resolutions into a seamless solution, virtually free of cracks and overlaps. The solution combines existing isosurface generation algorithms and wavelet theory to produce a real-time solution to multiple-resolution isosurfaces.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/m2/1/high_res_d/754498.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/","https://core.ac.uk/download/71192578.pdf","https://osti.gov/biblio/754498","https://osti.gov/servlets/purl/754498","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/?q=multiresolution volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/?q=marching cubes","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/?q=isosurface extraction","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/?q=marching cubes ambiguity","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/?q=isosurface rendering without mesh","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/?q=lorensen cline marching cubes","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc702274/?q=wavelet volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/6